  "id": "conjoint-therapy",
  "term": "conjoint therapy",
  "definition": "Conjoint therapy is a form of therapy in which both members of a couple take part together, treating difficulties in a shared relational context rather than focusing only on one person alone. In the packet, it is described as a dyadic approach for PTSD that aims to improve both trauma-related and relationship outcomes.",
